      "writtenOn": "2023-10-10T00:27:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Understood, but I think the code is doing something we still does not want.\n\nScenario 1:\n* User is connected to device A, then to device B.\n* User toggle bluetooth off / on\n* The order of connected device returned by getMostRecentlyConnectedDevices is [B,A] so the code autoconnect on B (first in list)\n\nScenario 2:\n* User is connected to device A, then to device B.\n* User turn off B\n* User toggle bluetooth off / on\n* The order of connected device returned by getMostRecentlyConnectedDevices is still [B,A] so the code autoconnect on B (first in list) but B is no longer an active device so there will be no device to connect to.\n\n\nIf we handle the case of device B being remotely disconnected we would have this new scenario:\n\nScenario 3:\n* User is connected to device A, then to device B.\n* User turn off B\n* User toggle bluetooth off / on\n* The order of connected device returned by getMostRecentlyConnectedDevices is [A] so the code autoconnect on A",
      "parentUuid": "15a7b060_6d6c2e45",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 652,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 652,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "662e4b3081a05304fc47c113d892745726503bbd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
